step_details.raw_response:
Thought: Test a simple mean over the full pool to gauge baseline performance.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using inverse error to see if it improves on the simple mean baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a robust median combination on the full pool to see if it beats the mean baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test a trimmed mean on the full pool to see if removing extremes improves over median.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Try a best_single strategy with ETS to see if a single top model beats the robust combinations.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"ETS"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using the pooled_meta_model handle (w1) on the full pool to see if a meta-weighted approach improves over the best single ETS.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"w1"}

Thought: Test a robust dba combination on the full pool to see if it beats the best single ETS.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool_full","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Try a weighted combination on the smaller, more stable pool1 using inverse_error to see if a focused weighted approach beats the best_single ETS.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool1","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on a different pool (pool2) to see if a more focused subset improves over the current best_single ETS.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool2","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a simple mean over a smaller, more stable pool (pool1) to see if restricting models improves performance.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on the smaller, stable pool1 using inverse_error weights to see if restricting to strong models improves over mean and median on that pool.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool1","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a median combination on the restricted, more stable pool1 to see if a robust aggregation over a few strong models can beat the best_single ETS baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool1"}

Thought: Test a simple mean combination over pool2 to see if expanding the pool improves over the best median pool1.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool2"}

